#: ../../source/testing/mocking.rst:3
msgid "Mocking System Classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/mocking.rst:5
msgid ""
"Several components within the framework provide mocked versions of their "
"classes that can be used during testing. These classes can take the place"
" of the normal class during test execution, often providing additional "
"assertions to test that actions have taken place (or not taken place) "
"during the execution of the test. This might be checking data gets cached"
" correctly, emails were sent correctly, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/mocking.rst:15
msgid "Cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/mocking.rst:17
msgid ""
"You can mock the cache with the ``mock()`` method, using the "
"``CacheFactory`` as its only parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/mocking.rst:21
msgid ""
"While this returns an instance of ``CodeIgniter\\Test\\Mock\\MockCache`` "
"that you can use directly, it also inserts the mock into the Service "
"class, so any calls within your code to ``service('cache')`` or "
"``Config\\Services::cache()`` will use the mocked class within its place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/mocking.rst:25
msgid ""
"When using this in more than one test method within a single file you "
"should call either the ``clean()`` or ``bypass()`` methods during the "
"test ``setUp()`` to ensure a clean slate when your tests run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/mocking.rst:29
msgid "Additional Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/mocking.rst:31
msgid ""
"You can instruct the mocked cache handler to never do any caching with "
"the ``bypass()`` method. This will emulate using the dummy handler and "
"ensures that your test does not rely on cached data for your tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/testing/mocking.rst:37
msgid "Available Assertions"
msgstr ""

